'''Marianne Fatton''' (born 16 December 1995) is a Swiss [[Ski mountaineering|ski mountaineer]]. She represented Switzerland at the [[2026 Winter Olympics]], and won a gold medal in the [[Ski mountaineering at the 2026 Winter Olympics#Medalists|sprint race]].

==Career==
Fatton competed at the [[2023 World Championship of Ski Mountaineering]] and won a silver medal in the sprint race with a time of 3:14.005.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.insidethegames.biz/articles/1134263/ski-mo-sprint-world-champs |title=Delight for first time champions in sprint events at Ski Mountaineering World Championships |website=[[insidethegames.biz]] |first=Philip |last=Barker |date=28 February 2023 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref>

In March 2025, she competed at the [[2025 World Championship of Ski Mountaineering]] and won a gold medal in the sprint race, with a time of 3:20.96. With the win, she earned a quota spot for the discipline at the [[2026 Winter Olympics]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.olympics.com/en/milano-cortina-2026/news/2025-ismf-ski-mountaineering-world-championships-marianne-fatton-oriol-cardona-coll-claim-sprint-world-titles-in-morgins-secure-milano-cortina-2026-quota-spots |title=2025 ISMF Ski Mountaineering World Championships: Marianne Fatton and Oriol Cardona Coll claim sprint world titles in Morgins, secure Milano Cortina 2026 quota spots |website=olympics.com |first=Nischal |last=Schwager-Patel |date=6 March 2025 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.insidethegames.biz/articles/1152265/first-skimo-spots-awarded-for-2026-games |title=First skimo 2026 spots awarded |website=[[insidethegames.biz]] |first=Elliot |last=McGowan |date=11 March 2025 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref> She also won a bronze medal in the mixed relay, along with [[Robin Bussard]], with a time of 33:02.9.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.olympics.com/en/milano-cortina-2026/news/2025-ismf-ski-mountaineering-world-championships-france-spain-quota-spots-milano-cortina-2026/ |title=2025 ISMF Ski Mountaineering World Championships: France and Spain finish 1-2 in mixed relay to secure quota spots Milano Cortina 2026 |website=olympics.com |first=Chloe |last=Merrell |date=3 March 2025 |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref>

On 19 February 2026, Fatton won the first-ever Olympic gold medal in [[Ski mountaineering at the Winter Olympics|ski mountaineering]], finishing in first place in the [[Ski mountaineering at the 2026 Winter Olympics – Women's sprint|sprint race]] with a time of 2:59.77.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://lasvegassun.com/news/2026/feb/19/ski-mountaineering-makes-its-olympic-debut-with-ma/ |title=Ski mountaineering makes its Olympic debut with Marianne Fatton of Switzerland winning the first gold medal |newspaper=[[Las Vegas Sun]] |date=19 February 2026 |access-date=19 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.olympics.com/en/milano-cortina-2026/news/winter-olympics-2026-ski-mountaineering-marianne-fatton-wins-skimo-first-olympic-gold-womens-sprint-milano-cortina-2026 |title=Winter Olympics 2026 ski mountaineering: Marianne Fatton wins Skimo’s first-ever Olympic gold in women’s sprint at Milano Cortina 2026 |website=olympics.com |first=Michael |last=Hincks |date=19 February 2026 |access-date=19 February 2026}}</ref> On 21 February 2026, she won a silver medal in the [[Ski mountaineering at the 2026 Winter Olympics – Mixed relay|mixed relay]], along with [[Jon Kistler]], with a time of 27:09.30.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bluewin.ch/en/sport/marianne-fatton-and-jon-kistler-win-silver-in-the-mixed-relay-3107683.html |title=Marianne Fatton and Jon Kistler win silver in the mixed relay |website=bluewin.ch |date=21 February 2026 |access-date=21 February 2026}}</ref>

==Personal life==
Fatton's mother, [[Anna Janoušková]], is a former Olympic [[Cross-country skiing (sport)|cross-country skier]] who competed at the [[1992 Winter Olympics]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://scarpa.com/pages/athlete/marianne-fatton |title=Marianne Fatton Ski Mountaineering as a Vocation |website=scarpa.com |access-date=29 December 2025}}</ref> 

